% Test cases for the negative pressure wound therapy policy (npwt.le):
% synthetic claims, one or two per criterion of LCD L33821 and per payment
% condition of Policy Article A52511, each stating only what its record
% shows. Findings are recorded as the treating practitioner's or the
% Council's. The queries: whether the claim is payable (the first query, so
% "stage" reads its checklist), whether it is reasonable and necessary, and
% what minimal change would make it payable.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base npwt cases includes these resources:
    npwt.

the knowledge base npwt cases includes:

query pay is:
    which claim is payable.

query rn is:
    which claim is reasonable and necessary.

query stage is:
    the query fails at which section.

query flip is:
    which minimal change to the scenario makes it the case that
        claim 1 is payable.

% A complete first-month claim for a pump under criterion A: a stage 4
% pressure ulcer on the pelvis present for 45 days, every measure of the
% wound therapy program tried, no exclusion; the order, delivery and proof
% of delivery (E2402 needs neither a face-to-face encounter nor prior
% authorization), the practitioner's initial statement and the diagnosis
% code.
scenario pump_complete is:
    claim 1 is for the pump.
    the HCPCS code of the pump is "E2402".
    the pump is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-05-01.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the pump is applied to the sacral ulcer.
    the sacral ulcer is a wound of Ann.
    the type of the sacral ulcer is pressure ulcer.
    the stage of the sacral ulcer is 4.
    the site of the sacral ulcer is pelvis.
    the sacral ulcer has been present for 45 days.
    the wound therapy program for the sacral ulcer included evaluation care and wound measurements by a licensed medical professional.
    the wound therapy program for the sacral ulcer included dressings to maintain a moist wound environment.
    the wound therapy program for the sacral ulcer included debridement of necrotic tissue present.
    the wound therapy program for the sacral ulcer included evaluation of and provision for adequate nutritional status.
    the wound therapy program for the sacral ulcer included appropriate turning and positioning.
    the wound therapy program for the sacral ulcer included appropriate management of moisture and incontinence.
    the wound therapy program for the sacral ulcer included use of a group 2 or 3 support surface.
    NPWT for the sacral ulcer was initiated on 2026-05-01.
    the treating practitioner documented the initial condition of the sacral ulcer with measurements and the wound care efforts.
    the diagnosis code of Ann is "L89.154".
    the order for the pump is dated 2026-04-25.
    the order for the pump is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the pump includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the pump includes order date.
    the order for the pump includes description of the item.
    the order for the pump includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the pump includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the pump was communicated to the supplier on 2026-04-27.
    the pump was delivered on 2026-05-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the pump.
    pay expects answers ["claim 1 is payable"].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers [].

